<title>UK: J. Bibby soars amid hopes for buyout.</title>
<headline>J. Bibby soars amid hopes for buyout.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in J. Bibby and Sons Plc soared 41 percent to a five-year high on Thursday, after the UK diversified industrials and trading group said it was in talks with Barlow Ltd.</p>
<p>J.Bibby said that the talks with the South African group could lead to Barlow making an offer for the 21.1 percent of Bibby it does not already own  nFLLFG603O.</p>
<p>By 1351 GMT, Bibby shares were up 53p to 181-1/2 on turnover of 1.27 million shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;I don't know what fair value would be, but I can tell you that no one seems to be chasing the shares up here,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
